  <h2 id="sales">Who pays for these skills, and how they judge you</h2>

  <p>
    Organisations pay for smoother processes, fewer errors and confident users. They judge you by clear documentation, tested changes and calm support.
  </p>
  <p>
    The first basic skill is drawing a process from request to result and spotting where it breaks.
  </p>

  <h2 id="ai">AI and ERP and business technology consulting: which tasks are under pressure</h2>

  <p>
    AI tools draft requirements, summarise tickets and generate test cases. Routine documentation shrinks.
  </p>
  <p>
    Process judgment, stakeholder trust and accountability hold value. A staged path helps: now, use AI to draft and check; later, own design decisions and user adoption.
  </p>

